# Integration Testing Layers

RULE: 5 testing layers, cumulative (Layer N+1 meaningless if Layer N fails). Each layer has a defined location, trigger, and credential requirement.
WHY: Prevents silent schema drift, infrastructure provisioning gaps, and pipeline wire mismatches from reaching production.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/integration-testing-layers.md (SSOT)

## Quick Reference

| Layer | What | Where | In quickmerge? | Credentials |
|-------|------|-------|----------------|-------------|
| 0 | Contract alignment (AC external↔internal schema pairs) | unified-api-contracts tests/ | Yes | None |
| 1 | Schema robustness (fail-fast, corner cases) | Each repo: tests/unit/test_schema_robustness.py | Yes | None |
| 1.5 | Per-component integration (adapter/event/config wiring with mocks) | Each repo: tests/integration/test_<component>_integration.py | Yes (blocking, last local gate) | None |
| 2 | Infrastructure verify (buckets, topics, IAM) | deployment-service/scripts/verify_infra.py | No (post-deploy) | GCP |
| 3a | Pipeline smoke (happy path, fast) | system-integration-tests/ `@pytest.mark.smoke` | No (post-deploy) | GCP sandbox |
| 3b | Full E2E (corner cases, auth, perf) | system-integration-tests/ `@pytest.mark.full_e2e` | No (post-deploy) | GCP sandbox |

## When Writing Tests

Layer 0: If you change a schema in UAC (external or internal), add or update a contract alignment test in unified-api-contracts.
Layer 1: If you add/change a Pydantic model any service consumes, add test_schema_robustness.py tests.
Layer 1.5: If you add/change a service adapter, EventSink wiring, or config loading, add a component integration test with mocked dependencies.
Layer 2: If you add a new GCS bucket or PubSub topic, add it to verify_infra.py resource list.
Layer 3: If you add a new service-to-service data flow, add a smoke test in system-integration-tests.

DO:
  Layer 0 in UAC (unified-api-contracts); Layer 1 per-service; Layer 1.5 per-service (tests/integration/); Layer 2 in deployment-service; Layer 3 in system-integration-tests
  Sequential: 3a passes before 3b runs
  system-integration-tests interacts via HTTP/GCS/PubSub only — zero Python imports from services
  Layer 1.5: mock all external dependencies (no live GCS, no live PubSub, no live Secret Manager)
  Run Layer 1.5: `pytest tests/integration/ -v --timeout=30`

## Private Dependency Integration Tests (Layer 1.5 — Required)

Every repo that lists internal unified_* packages as dependencies MUST have Layer 1.5 integration tests:

- Location: `tests/integration/test_<dep_name>_integration.py`
- Use `unittest.mock` or `pytest-mock` — NO live cloud calls
- Test the actual wiring: config loading, adapter init, event emission, schema round-trip
- One test file per private dependency boundary

```python
# Example: testing unified-trading-library dep wiring with mocks
@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
def mock_cloud_clients():
    with patch("unified_cloud_interface.get_storage_client") as mock_storage, \
         patch("unified_cloud_interface.get_secret_client") as mock_secret:
        mock_storage.return_value = MagicMock(spec=StorageClient)
        mock_secret.return_value = MagicMock(spec=SecretClient)
        yield mock_storage, mock_secret

def test_service_initialises_with_utl_deps(mock_cloud_clients):
    # Real import, mocked I/O — Layer 1.5 pattern
    svc = MyService(config=MyConfig.model_validate({"ENV": "test", ...}))
    assert svc.is_ready()
```

## External Interface VCR Tests (Layer 1 — Required for Interface Repos)

The active external-facing interface and service repos MUST have VCR-recorded integration tests:
- unified-market-interface
- execution-service (contains CeFi/DeFi/sports execution — formerly unified-trade-execution-interface, unified-defi-execution-interface, unified-sports-execution-interface)
- instruments-service (contains reference data — formerly unified-reference-data-interface)
- position-balance-monitor-service (contains position interface — formerly unified-position-interface)

VCR cassettes live in: `unified-api-contracts/unified_api_contracts/unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/mocks/<endpoint>.yaml`

```python
import vcr
from pathlib import Path

CASSETTE_DIR = Path("../unified-api-contracts/unified_api_contracts/unified_api_contracts_external")

@vcr.use_cassette(str(CASSETTE_DIR / "binance/mocks/ticker_24hr.yaml"))
def test_binance_ticker_validates_against_ac_schema():
    # Real HTTP call recorded in cassette — validates against AC schema
    from unified_api_contracts.binance.schemas import BinanceTicker24hr
    response = adapter.fetch_ticker("BTCUSDT")
    BinanceTicker24hr.model_validate(response)  # fails if schema drifts
```

Re-record cassettes when venue API changes. Store cassettes in unified-api-contracts only (never copy to consumers).

NEVER:
  Layer 3 tests that import service internals (creates cross-service Python dependency)
  Skip Layer 0 when modifying schemas ("it's just a field rename")
  Put infra verification in quickmerge (needs cloud credentials)
  Use live cloud resources in Layer 1.5 (belongs in Layer 2+)
